    </node><node id="re30"><data key="dcells">COX-1: platelets, lung mast cells, endothelium. COX-2: blood monocytes and synovial fibroblasts after a cytokine or endotoxin (human, product measured)</data><data key="dsite">luminal face of the endoplasmic reticulum and the nuclear envelope. COX-1 sits evenly in both, COX-2 twice as much in the envelope, and an active COX-2 pool is on the Golgi as well</data><data key="dref">pubmed:29225187 pubmed:1907252 pubmed:1380156 pubmed:7738031 pubmed:25548276 pubmed:10381787 pubmed:333448 pubmed:11095985 pubmed:12233875</data><data key="ng">
